From fd9f8b607e3a67a01079bfed43f376335e19243e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:39:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Signal solves in the layout of the native kernel: no
 transposed copies

The native kernel factorizes and solves on arrays with one row per unknown,
shape (m, F). The forward pass handed it right-hand sides of shape (F, m, k)
instead, which plu_solve_fmk copies into a work array and back for every
right-hand side, and then transposed the solutions once more for signal and
again in the reverse pass for conj(Y) and MU.

Now the right-hand sides, which are zero outside a few rows, are handed over
as rows and values (solve_scattered). The native kernel builds them in its own
layout and returns (m, F) solutions directly; the SuperLU path builds its
(F, m, k) array as before. The adjoint helpers are kept as conj(Y) and MU with
one row per unknown, the layout the reverse pass works in, so its two
transposed copies are gone on both paths. The noise sums run in the same
layout, and the cotangent of the noise entries is only formed for the entries
that come from noise functions.

Emulated x86-64 with the native kernel, 6 alternating runs: warm forward
18.8 -> 17.1 ms, warm gradient 4.8 -> 4.5 ms; page faults of the first calls
5703 -> 5036 (forward) and 1997 -> 1516 (backward). Benchmark outputs and
gradient bit-identical there. On arm64 (SuperLU path) carrier, signal, noise,
sensitivity and powers are bit-identical and the gradient agrees to 4e-16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 differometor/__pycache__/fast.cpython-312.pyc | Bin 109728 -> 112060 bytes
 differometor/fast.py                          | 147 +++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

